              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">12 months</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Common recalibration interval for regular use</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="common-specs" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Common Torque Specs Around the Garage
          </h2>

          <p>
            Always use the number in the service manual or the owner's manual for your exact vehicle or part. The ranges below are typical values to help you choose a wrench size, not specifications to tighten anything to. Wheels in particular vary by make, stud size and wheel material, and aftermarket wheels sometimes carry their own specification.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Fastener</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical range</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Wrench to use</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
